    "result_text": "All changes compile and the full test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`). The audit output confirms the new behaviour end-to-end:\n\n```\n{\"seq\":1,\"schemaVersion\":2,\"ownerId\":11,\"memberId\":\"NSWV22616E6609E9\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\n## What I changed and why\n\n**Version-2 identity derivation** \u2014 a single shared source of truth for the version tag:\n- `util/IdentityVersion.java` (new): `TAG = \"V2\"` (mixed into identifiers) and `VERSION = 2` (surfaced as `apiVersion`/`schemaVersion`).\n- `util/IdentityRegionCode.java` (new): `v2(region)` produces the region code used *inside* identifiers (`\"NSW\"` \u2192 `\"NSWV2\"`), keeping tag-mixing out of the service.\n- `HouseholdIdGenerator` / `OwnerIdentityKey`: append `|V2` to their SHA-256 pre-images, so every digest differs from V1.\n- `ClinicServiceImpl.assignMemberId`: the memberId's region is now `IdentityRegionCode.v2(...)`, so the memberId string (`NSWV226\u2026`) can never collide with a V1 memberId (`NSW26\u2026`).\n\n**Keeping `locality` plain (tag only inside identifiers)** \u2014 the user-facing fields no longer read the region back out of the (now tagged) memberId:\n- Removed the now-dead `LocalityResolver.fromMemberId` and `MemberIdGenerator.region`.\n- `OwnerMapper` derives `locality`/`timezone` from plain `LocalityResolver.resolve(city, postcode)`.\n- Added `OwnerSegment.of(Owner)` so the plain-region segment derivation lives in one place, reused by both the mapper and the audit logger.\n\n**Response shape** (`openapi.yml` \u2192 regenerated DTOs):\n- New `OwnerIdentity` schema grouping `memberId`/`householdId`/`identityKey`; the flat top-level fields are removed.\n- `Owner` gains `identity` (nested) and integer `apiVersion` (both required); mapper wires them via `toOwnerIdentityDto(owner)` and `IdentityVersion.VERSION`.\n\n**Audit schema v2** (`OwnerCreatedEvent` + `OwnerAuditLogger`): added `schemaVersion: 2` and an `ownerSegment` recomputed from the owner via the shared `OwnerSegment.of`.\n\nRequest fields (`OwnerFields`) are untouched, as specified.",
