    "probe_text": "Here is every validation and side-effect applied when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`, in the order they execute. The endpoint is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:118`), which delegates to `ClinicServiceImpl.createOwner`.\n\n## Validations (in execution order)\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` on the controller. Caller must have the `OWNER_ADMIN` role or the request is rejected before the body runs.\n\n2. **Bean Validation on the request body** (`@Valid OwnerFieldsDto`, failures \u2192 400):\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `title` \u2014 `@Pattern(^(MR|MRS|MS|DR)$)`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `addressLine1` \u2014 `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)`, `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`, plus custom `@TelephoneDigits` (must be normalizable to E.164)\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Email`, `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`\n   - `registrationDate` \u2014 `@PastOrPresent`\n\n3. **Class-level custom validators on the DTO** (part of step 2, \u2192 400):\n   - `@ValidPostcodeForCity` \u2014 a well-formed 4-digit postcode must be valid for the city's region.\n   - `@ValidAddressForm` \u2014 either `addressLine1` or the flat `address` must be non-blank.\n\n4. **Service-layer business validations** (`ClinicServiceImpl.createOwner`, `service/ClinicServiceImpl.java:280`):\n   - **Disposable email** \u2014 `DisposableEmailDomains.isDisposable(email)` \u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException` (400).\n   - **Identity-key collision** \u2014 `rejectIdentityCollision`: among active (non-soft-deleted) owners sharing the normalized telephone, rejects if any matches full identity key (telephone + lowercased email + last-name Soundex) \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerException` (409).\n   - **Per-city capacity** \u2014 if `countByCity(city) >= 50` \u2192 `CityCapacityExceededException` (409).\n   - **Per-day limit** \u2014 if `countByRegistrationDate(...) >= 100` \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` (429).\n\n5. **Entity-level constraints enforced on flush** \u2014 `@NotEmpty` on `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`; `@NotEmpty @Pattern(^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$)` on `telephone`.\n\n## Side-effects (in execution order)\n\n1. **Idempotency replay check** (before any work) \u2014 if the `Idempotency-Key` header matches a previously created owner, the original owner is returned with **200 OK** and nothing new happens.\n\n2. **Field normalization during DTO\u2192entity mapping** (`OwnerMapper.toOwner`): `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` normalized, `address` composed from the lines, `telephone` converted to E.164, `email` normalized; `id` and `pets` ignored.\n\n3. **Derived fields computed and set on the entity** (in `createOwner`, before save):\n   - `householdId` \u2014 generated from last name + postcode\n   - `capacityWarning` \u2014 true if city count \u2265 40\n   - `registrationDate` \u2014 defaulted to today if null, then adjusted to a business day\n   - `bulkSignupWarning` \u2014 true if same-day count > 80\n   - `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` \u2014 soft-match flag (skipped when `sharesHousehold` is true; needs a postcode)\n   - `namesakeCount` \u2014 count of existing same first+last name owners\n   - `householdSize` \u2014 household members + 1\n   - `membershipLevel` \u2014 capped level based on household\n   - `memberId` \u2014 assigned from region/date/telephone/last name, de-duplicated\n\n4. **Persist** \u2014 `ownerRepository.save(owner)`; DB-generated identity id.\n\n5. **Idempotency registry update** \u2014 remembers the key \u2192 new owner id.\n\n6. **Audit** \u2014 `OwnerAuditLogger.ownerCreated`: emits a human-readable line plus a structured JSON `OwnerCreatedEvent` (with incrementing sequence number) to the `AUDIT` logger.\n\n7. **Notification** \u2014 `WelcomeNotifier.welcome`: logs a \"welcome enqueued\" line to the `NOTIFY` logger (log stub, no real email).\n\n8. **HTTP response** \u2014 returns **201 Created** with a `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header and the owner body.\n\nNotably, there are **no JPA lifecycle callbacks** (`@PrePersist` etc.) and **no Spring application events** in this path \u2014 all side-effects are explicit in the service method."
